From 9629aa043b608153ad1faf085e2806715636398a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 03:40:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add the print-controller family (unblocks PrintPreviewDialog)

Restores the System.Drawing.Printing controllers, absent until now:

- PrintController (abstract base: IsPreview, OnStartPrint/OnStartPage/OnEndPage/
  OnEndPrint).
- StandardPrintController - returns the print loop's page graphics.
- PreviewPrintController - actually captures each page into a bitmap and exposes
  them via GetPreviewPageInfo(); has UseAntiAlias. This is what PrintPreviewDialog
  needs.
- PreviewPageInfo (Image + PhysicalSize), InvalidPrinterException (: SystemException).
- PrintControllerWithStatusDialog (System.Windows.Forms) - delegates to an
  underlying controller; the status dialog is not shown on GTK.
- PrintDocument gains its PrintController property (defaulting to
  StandardPrintController), via a new partial.

Net48 Drawing types present 136->141, Forms 911->912. Full suite green at 2357
(+6 tests, including a real preview-capture cycle). The printing test seeds GTK
via the Form static constructor before creating Bitmap/Graphics/PrinterSettings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
